<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fidesz</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fidesz – Hungarian Civic Alliance</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fidesz is a Hungarian political party founded in 1988 as a liberal alliance of young democrats, which under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viktor-orban">Viktor Orbán</a> moved to national conservatism. It governed from 1998 to 2002 and won a two-thirds majority in 2010, which it used to adopt a new constitution, the Fundamental Law of 2011. It repeated its two-thirds majorities in later elections.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fidesz.jpg" alt="Fidesz" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fidesz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fidesz_2015.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
